<rml>
<head>
    <title>Desktop Melee</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="welcome.rcss" />
</head>
<!-- Desktop Melee's welcome window on Windows and Linux
     (docs/desktop-melee/ui-guide.md sections 9 to 11). One page per step;
     desktop-melee/src/welcome_window.cpp shows one at a time, fills in the
     values and handles every click by id. -->
<body>
    <div id="top">
        <span class="title">Desktop Melee</span>
        <span id="counter"></span>
    </div>

    <div id="body">
        <div id="step-welcome" class="step">
            <div id="sketch">
                <div class="edge left"></div><div class="edge right"></div>
                <div class="fighter p1"></div><div class="fighter p2"></div>
                <div class="panel"></div>
            </div>
            <h1>Desktop Melee</h1>
            <p class="lead">Real Melee, played right on your desktop. Your panel is the stage, and the edges of the screen are the blast zones.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="step-disc" class="step">
            <h1 id="disc-title">Bring your own Melee</h1>
            <p id="disc-lead" class="lead">Desktop Melee includes the game's code but none of Nintendo's data. Characters, stages and sound come from your own copy of Melee.</p>
            <div id="drop">
                <p class="big">Drop your disc image here</p>
                <p class="types">Melee USA 1.02:  .iso  .gcm  .ciso  .rvz</p>
                <button id="choose" class="secondary">Choose file...</button>
            </div>
            <div id="disc-status">
                <p id="disc-line" class="line"></p>
                <div id="disc-bar" class="bar hidden"><div id="disc-fill" class="fill"></div></div>
                <p id="disc-name" class="name"></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="step-loading" class="step">
            <h1>Getting Melee ready...</h1>
            <p id="loading-lead" class="lead">The first launch builds Melee's graphics, so matches never stutter. It takes a few minutes, once. You can use your computer in the meantime.</p>
            <div class="bar"><div id="loading-fill" class="fill"></div></div>
            <p id="loading-count" class="small"></p>
        </div>

        <div id="step-controls" class="step">
            <h1>Grab a controller</h1>
            <div id="cards">
                <div id="card-gamecube" class="card"><p class="name">GameCube</p><p class="sub">Official adapter, or one in Wii U mode</p></div>
                <div id="card-pad" class="card"><p class="name">Xbox, PS, Switch</p><p class="sub">USB or Bluetooth</p></div>
                <div id="card-keyboard" class="card"><p class="name">Keyboard</p><p id="keys-toggle" class="sub">Show the keys</p></div>
            </div>
            <div id="keys" class="hidden"></div>
            <p class="listen-title">PRESS ANY BUTTON</p>
            <div id="pressed"></div>
            <p class="small">Press a button on each controller, or a key, to see who's who. Ports can be changed in the settings window's Controls tab.</p>
            <p class="small">The keyboard works while the game window is in front: click it before pressing keys.</p>
        </div>

        <div id="step-done" class="step">
            <div id="tray-sketch">
                <span class="spacer"></span>
                <div class="icon"><div class="floor"></div><div class="f1"></div><div class="f2"></div></div>
                <span>12:00</span>
            </div>
            <h1>You're set</h1>
            <p class="lead">Desktop Melee lives in your system tray. Use it to pick characters, change controls and start a match.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="bottom">
        <button id="next" class="primary">Get started</button>
        <p id="or-start" class="hidden">or press Start on your controller</p>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
